                <pb facs="0640" n="568" xml:id="pg568"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 10044/151A.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Ambassador Leishman.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1909-04-21"><hi rendition="#italic">April 21,
                        1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Knox informs Mr. Leishman that the <hi rendition="#italic">Montana</hi> and
                        <hi rendition="#italic">North Carolina</hi> will proceed immediately from
                    Guantanamo to the Mediterranean, waiting at Gibraltar for orders.</p>
            </div>
